> Anyone have any tips about Samurais? What to do, what to use.. I think I got
> the hang of it, but I'm probably missing stuff.

Don't bother getting your short sword skill up. Invest in long sword
(katana) skill and in two-weaponing. Start sacrificing as soon as
possible until you get Snickersnee, which is a katana and your
guaranteed first weapon. Then two-weapon Snickersnee and your original
katana. If you can get Frosty early, even better - both Brands, being
long swords, use the same skill as your katanas. Failing that, you can
dip for Excalibur if you like. It's a bit better than Snickersnee, but
not nearly as good as a Brand.
Once you get a silver saber, it might be worth getting that up, too, for
Gehennom, but getting enough skill to reach Gehennom in the first place
is more important...
Don't bother with your quest artifact, either. It may be a big bad
two-handed sword, but it's no patch on two well-enchanted long swords or
katanas. But be careful that you don't give your quest nemesis a chance
to cut you in half.
Do not forget your bow. It isn't going to be your most important weapon,
but at the start of the game it can be very useful indeed for killing
floating eyes, gelatinous blobs, blue jellies, 'trices and all those odd
beasties you don't want to touch. Very useful for those monsters stuck
behind boulders, too (Sokoban!). Untrap arrow traps (or milk them, but
you aren't going to need hundreds of arrows like a ranger, because it's
only an occasional weapon for you) and save your ya for the harder
monsters - you can easily kill a sessile monster with ordinary arrows.

